{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat ../direct-checks/66acce1428c3477f8a6c0f0d1ea19ee1/omnipaxos/tests/assurance_generated.rs; grep CA_EVENT ../logs/eb1ca4d437f64ec8882a7005a78fb321/stdout.log; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('../direct-checks/66acce1428c3477f8a6c0f0d1ea19ee1/plan.json'));p['harness'].pop('source');print(json.dumps(p,indent=2))\ns=json.load(open('../state.json'))\nfor col in ['claims','bindings','monitor_results']:\n for x in s[col]:\n  if x.get('id') in ['claim-storage-error-rollback','binding-storage-rollback'] or x.get('experiment_check_id')=='eb1ca4d437f64ec8882a7005a78fb321':print(col,json.dumps(x,indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat ../direct-checks/66acce1428c3477f8a6c0f0d1ea19ee1/omnipaxos/tests/assurance_generated.rs; grep CA_EVENT ../logs/eb1ca4d437f64ec8882a7005a78fb321/stdout.log; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('../direct-checks/66acce1428c3477f8a6c0f0d1ea19ee1/plan.json'));p['harness'].pop('source');print(json.dumps(p,indent=2))\ns=json.load(open('../state.json'))\nfor col in ['claims','bindings','monitor_results']:\n for x in s[col]:\n  if x.get('id') in ['claim-storage-error-rollback','binding-storage-rollback'] or x.get('experiment_check_id')=='eb1ca4d437f64ec8882a7005a78fb321':print(col,json.dumps(x,indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"use omnipaxos::{ballot_leader_election::Ballot, storage::{Entry, NoSnapshot, Storage, StorageOp}};\nuse omnipaxos_storage::persistent_storage::{PersistentStorage, PersistentStorageConfig};\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize, Serializer};\nuse serde_json::json;\nuse std::sync::atomic::{AtomicUsize, Ordering};\n\nstatic SERIALIZATION_ERRORS: AtomicUsize = AtomicUsize::new(0);\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Deserialize, PartialEq)]\nstruct Value(u64);\nimpl Serialize for Value {\n    fn serialize<S: Serializer>(&self, serializer: S) -> Result<S::Ok, S::Error> {\n        if self.0 == 999 {\n            SERIALIZATION_ERRORS.fetch_add(1, Ordering::SeqCst);\n            return Err(serde::ser::Error::custom(\"selected entry cannot be serialized\"));\n        }\n        serializer.serialize_u64(self.0)\n    }\n}\nimpl Entry for Value { type Snapshot = NoSnapshot; }\nfn event(v: serde_json::Value) { println!(\"CA_EVENT {}\", v); }\n\n#[test]\nfn persistent_returned_error_rollback() {\n    // Database lives only in this clean execution workspace; close before cleanup.\n    let root = tempfile::Builder::new().prefix(\"rollback-check-\").tempdir_in(\".\").unwrap();\n    let path = root.path().join(\"db\").to_string_lossy().into_owned();\n    let config = || PersistentStorageConfig::with_path(path.clone());\n    let mut storage = PersistentStorage::<Value>::open(config());\n    let old_ballot=Ballot::with(1,1,0,1);\n    let failed_ballot=Ballot::with(1,2,0,1);\n    storage.append_entry(Value(7)).unwrap();\n    storage.set_promise(old_ballot).unwrap();\n    let before_len=storage.get_log_len().unwrap();\n    let before_promise=storage.get_promise().unwrap().unwrap();\n    let before_prefix=storage.get_entries(0,before_len).unwrap();\n    assert_eq!(before_len,1);\n    assert_eq!(before_promise,old_ballot);\n    assert_eq!(before_prefix,vec![Value(7)]);\n    event(json!({\"event\":\"storage_admitted\",\"op_id\":\"failed-transaction\",\"before_len\":before_len,\n        \"before_promise_n\":before_promise.n,\"before_first\":before_prefix[0].0,\"error_value\":999}));\n    let result=storage.write_atomically(vec![StorageOp::SetPromise(failed_ballot),\n        StorageOp::AppendEntry(Value(11)),StorageOp::AppendEntry(Value(999))]);\n    let returned_error=result.is_err();\n    let error_count=SERIALIZATION_ERRORS.load(Ordering::SeqCst);\n    let error_text=result.err().map(|e|e.to_string()).unwrap_or_default();\n    event(json!({\"event\":\"storage_returned\",\"op_id\":\"failed-transaction\",\"returned_error\":returned_error,\n        \"serialization_error_observed\":error_count>0,\"error_text\":error_text}));\n    assert!(returned_error && error_count>0,\"selected serialization failure was not reached\");\n    let immediate_len=storage.get_log_len().unwrap();\n    let immediate_promise=storage.get_promise().unwrap().unwrap();\n    let prefix=storage.get_entries(0,1).unwrap();\n    event(json!({\"event\":\"immediate_state\",\"op_id\":\"failed-transaction\",\"log_len\":immediate_len,\n        \"promise_n\":immediate_promise.n,\"first\":prefix[0].0}));\n    // This independent transaction contains neither failed append nor failed promise.\n    let independent=storage.write_atomically(vec![StorageOp::SetDecidedIndex(0)]);\n    let independent_ok=independent.is_ok();\n    event(json!({\"event\":\"independent_completed\",\"op_id\":\"failed-transaction\",\"success\":independent_ok,\n        \"requested_decided_idx\":0}));\n    independent.unwrap();\n    let after_len=storage.get_log_len().unwrap();\n    let after_promise=storage.get_promise().unwrap().unwrap();\n    let after_entries=storage.get_entries(0,after_len).unwrap();\n    event(json!({\"event\":\"after_independent\",\"op_id\":\"failed-transaction\",\"log_len\":after_len,\n        \"promise_n\":after_promise.n,\"entries\":after_entries.iter().map(|v|v.0).collect::<Vec<_>>(),\n        \"decided_idx\":storage.get_decided_idx().unwrap()}));\n    drop(storage);\n    let reopened=PersistentStorage::<Value>::open(config());\n    let reopened_len=reopened.get_log_len().unwrap();\n    let reopened_promise=reopened.get_promise().unwrap().unwrap();\n    event(json!({\"event\":\"reopened_state\",\"op_id\":\"failed-transaction\",\"log_len\":reopened_len,\n        \"promise_n\":reopened_promise.n,\"entries\":reopened.get_entries(0,reopened_len).unwrap().iter().map(|v|v.0).collect::<Vec<_>>()}));\n    drop(reopened);\n    root.close().unwrap();\n}\ntest persistent_returned_error_rollback ... CA_EVENT {\"before_first\":7,\"before_len\":1,\"before_promise_n\":1,\"error_value\":999,\"event\":\"storage_admitted\",\"op_id\":\"failed-transaction\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"error_text\":\"selected entry cannot be serialized\",\"event\":\"storage_returned\",\"op_id\":\"failed-transaction\",\"returned_error\":true,\"serialization_error_observed\":true}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"immediate_state\",\"first\":7,\"log_len\":2,\"op_id\":\"failed-transaction\",\"promise_n\":1}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"independent_completed\",\"op_id\":\"failed-transaction\",\"requested_decided_idx\":0,\"success\":true}\nCA_EVENT {\"decided_idx\":0,\"entries\":[7,11],\"event\":\"after_independent\",\"log_len\":2,\"op_id\":\"failed-transaction\",\"promise_n\":2}\nCA_EVENT {\"entries\":[7,11],\"event\":\"reopened_state\",\"log_len\":2,\"op_id\":\"failed-transaction\",\"promise_n\":2}\n{\n  \"description\": \"Fixed direct PersistentStorage API check of returned-error rollback. After successful initial entry 7 and ballot 1, submit promise ballot 2, append 11, then an entry 999 whose Serialize returns Err. Observe live length immediately, execute an unrelated SetDecidedIndex(0) transaction, read database promise/log, close and reopen. Two comparisons test distinct observables of the same rollback responsibility.\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-storage-error-rollback\",\n  \"binding_ids\": [\n    \"binding-storage-rollback\"\n  ],\n  \"harness\": {\n    \"execution_package\": \"./omnipaxos\",\n    \"files\": {},\n    \"kind\": \"rust_test\",\n    \"description\": \"Actual PersistentStorage backed by RocksDB in a unique execution-workspace directory, with a user-defined Entry serializer returning a deterministic ordinary error for one selected value. No backend or dependency code modifications, no process crash or private access. The database is closed before cleanup. Prerequisite events identify successful setup and actual selected error; subsequent transaction success is checked in code and retained as a diagnostic event before the later result.\",\n    \"semantic_changes\": [\n      \"Use the public Entry serialization extension point to supply a returned error; all other entry values serialize normally.\",\n      \"Direct backend calls isolate the explicit Storage interface contract; no claim that the whole Paxos core continues after its storage panic.\",\n      \"Observe get_log_len from the live object and promise/entry data from backend public readers, then reopen as a diagnostic.\"\n    ],\n    \"prerequisites\": [\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"admitted\",\n        \"event\": \"storage_admitted\",\n        \"conditions\": []\n      },\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"failed\",\n        \"event\": \"storage_returned\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"op_id\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": null,\n            \"reference\": \"admitted.op_id\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"returned_error\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": true,\n            \"reference\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"serialization_error_observed\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": true,\n            \"reference\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"legality\": {\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-storage-contract\",\n        \"s-entry-contract\",\n        \"s-persistent-open\",\n        \"s-persistent-batch\",\n        \"s-persistent-atomic\",\n        \"s-persistent-read\"\n      ],\n      \"expectation_ids\": [\n        \"s-storage-contract\"\n      ],\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"binding-storage-rollback\"\n      ],\n      \"derivation\": \"The direct Storage interface owes all-or-rollback on returned Err. Setup persists one entry and a promise, then the submitted batch queues a new promise and a good append before a final entry serializer returns a normal error. Public reads sample live cursor and database metadata; a following transaction changes only decided index, so failed promise/appends must remain absent. Reopen distinguishes persistent effects from live cursor alone.\",\n      \"applicability\": \"One isolated persistent database, successful setup and ordinary I/O, no crashes or concurrency; Entry serialization can return Err through the implemented trait.\",\n      \"unresolved\": [],\n      \"conflicts\": [],\n      \"alternatives\": [\n        \"The database itself may remain unchanged at the initial Err even when the cursor changed; both are observed separately.\",\n        \"Dropping the object before reuse may discard pending writes; this check explicitly covers a live backend under its returned-error contract.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"monitors\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"monitor-rollback-live-length\",\n      \"checker_id\": \"rollback-live-length\",\n      \"event\": \"immediate_state\",\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"binding-storage-rollback\"\n      ],\n      \"grounding\": {\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"s-storage-contract\",\n          \"s-entry-contract\",\n          \"s-persistent-open\",\n          \"s-persistent-batch\",\n          \"s-persistent-atomic\",\n          \"s-persistent-read\"\n        ],\n        \"expectation_ids\": [\n          \"s-storage-contract\"\n        ],\n        \"binding_ids\": [\n          \"binding-storage-rollback\"\n        ],\n        \"derivation\": \"The direct Storage interface owes all-or-rollback on returned Err. Setup persists one entry and a promise, then the submitted batch queues a new promise and a good append before a final entry serializer returns a normal error. Public reads sample live cursor and database metadata; a following transaction changes only decided index, so failed promise/appends must remain absent. Reopen distinguishes persistent effects from live cursor alone.\",\n        \"applicability\": \"One isolated persistent database, successful setup and ordinary I/O, no crashes or concurrency; Entry serialization can return Err through the implemented trait.\",\n        \"unresolved\": [],\n        \"conflicts\": [],\n        \"alternatives\": [\n          \"The database itself may remain unchanged at the initial Err even when the cursor changed; both are observed separately.\",\n          \"Dropping the object before reuse may discard pending writes; this check explicitly covers a live backend under its returned-error contract.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"applicability_conditions\": [],\n      \"admission_alias\": \"admitted\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"monitor-rollback-later-promise\",\n      \"checker_id\": \"rollback-later-promise\",\n      \"event\": \"after_independent\",\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"binding-storage-rollback\"\n      ],\n      \"grounding\": {\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"s-storage-contract\",\n          \"s-entry-contract\",\n          \"s-persistent-open\",\n          \"s-persistent-batch\",\n          \"s-persistent-atomic\",\n          \"s-persistent-read\"\n        ],\n        \"expectation_ids\": [\n          \"s-storage-contract\"\n        ],\n        \"binding_ids\": [\n          \"binding-storage-rollback\"\n        ],\n        \"derivation\": \"The direct Storage interface owes all-or-rollback on returned Err. Setup persists one entry and a promise, then the submitted batch queues a new promise and a good append before a final entry serializer returns a normal error. Public reads sample live cursor and database metadata; a following transaction changes only decided index, so failed promise/appends must remain absent. Reopen distinguishes persistent effects from live cursor alone.\",\n        \"applicability\": \"One isolated persistent database, successful setup and ordinary I/O, no crashes or concurrency; Entry serialization can return Err through the implemented trait.\",\n        \"unresolved\": [],\n        \"conflicts\": [],\n        \"alternatives\": [\n          \"The database itself may remain unchanged at the initial Err even when the cursor changed; both are observed separately.\",\n          \"Dropping the object before reuse may discard pending writes; this check explicitly covers a live backend under its returned-error contract.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"applicability_conditions\": [],\n      \"admission_alias\": \"admitted\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"observable_properties\": [\n    {\n      \"checker_id\": \"rollback-live-length\",\n      \"kind\": \"event_assertion\",\n      \"trigger\": {\n        \"field\": \"event\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": \"immediate_state\",\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"assertion\": {\n        \"field\": \"log_len\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": null,\n        \"reference\": \"admitted.before_len\"\n      },\n      \"antecedent\": null,\n      \"identity_fields\": [\n        \"op_id\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Failed write_atomically must preserve the corresponding pre-call observable; subsequent unrelated successful transaction must not publish failed writes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"checker_id\": \"rollback-later-promise\",\n      \"kind\": \"event_assertion\",\n      \"trigger\": {\n        \"field\": \"event\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": \"after_independent\",\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"assertion\": {\n        \"field\": \"promise_n\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": null,\n        \"reference\": \"admitted.before_promise_n\"\n      },\n      \"antecedent\": null,\n      \"identity_fields\": [\n        \"op_id\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Failed write_atomically must preserve the corresponding pre-call observable; subsequent unrelated successful transaction must not publish failed writes.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"uncertainties\": [\n    \"Compilation of the default omnipaxos target enables its existing persistent-storage dev dependency; preparation is not semantic evidence.\",\n    \"No cluster consequence, crash recovery failure, or RocksDB atomic-commit failure is inferred from a local backend contract violation.\",\n    \"Reopened state is retained as diagnostic corroboration of persistence after the later successful call, not a separate requirement.\"\n  ]\n}\nclaims {\n  \"id\": \"claim-storage-error-rollback\",\n  \"kind\": \"obligation\",\n  \"concern\": \"implementation_semantics\",\n  \"description\": \"When Storage::write_atomically returns Err, the storage state exposed to its caller must equal the pre-call state, and a later independent successful transaction must not commit operations retained from the failed call.\",\n  \"scope\": {\n    \"description\": \"PersistentStorage direct Storage API use on a live backend with a deterministic returned entry-serialization error after earlier operations were prepared.\",\n    \"assumptions\": [\n      \"Entry implements the required Entry, Serialize and Deserialize interfaces; serialization error is returned normally, not panic.\",\n      \"Successful database initialization and I/O outside the selected error; no concurrent writers or compaction.\"\n    ],\n    \"excluded\": [\n      \"No claim of a legal whole-cluster history continuing after a core storage panic.\",\n      \"No crash, power-loss durability, RocksDB write failure or application endpoint is tested.\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": {}\n  },\n  \"source\": \"Candidate derived from attributed implementation responsibilities\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"s-storage-contract\",\n    \"s-persistent-atomic\"\n  ],\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"assessment\": \"unassessed\",\n  \"candidate\": true,\n  \"grounding\": {\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"s-storage-contract\",\n      \"s-persistent-atomic\"\n    ],\n    \"expectation_ids\": [],\n    \"binding_ids\": [\n      \"binding-storage-rollback\"\n    ],\n    \"derivation\": \"Storage::write_atomically explicitly requires all operations or rollback, with Err assumed rolled back to state before the call. PersistentStorage implements this trait and propagates entry serialization errors as Err without an advertised poisoning restriction. Public reads immediately after return test the state guarantee; a later unrelated transaction tests whether failed operations remain pending. The core relies on this backend during sync, but the obligation stays at the storage interface.\",\n    \"applicability\": \"Direct public calls to the captured persistent backend using a trait-conforming entry with a controlled serializer error.\",\n    \"unresolved\": [],\n    \"conflicts\": [],\n    \"alternatives\": [\n      \"Dropping and reopening may restore state, but that is not the stated return-time rollback guarantee.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"version\": 1\n}\nbindings {\n  \"associations\": [\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-storage-error-rollback\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-storage-contract\",\n        \"s-persistent-atomic\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"The trait requirement applies directly to this implementation.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"anchor\": {\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"s-persistent-atomic\"\n    ],\n    \"boundary_complete\": true,\n    \"kind\": \"declaration\",\n    \"material_id\": \"s-persistent-atomic\",\n    \"start_line\": 278,\n    \"end_line\": 278,\n    \"symbol\": \"write_atomically\"\n  },\n  \"material_id\": \"s-persistent-atomic\",\n  \"id\": \"binding-storage-rollback\",\n  \"file\": \"omnipaxos_storage/src/persistent_storage.rs\",\n  \"symbol\": \"write_atomically\",\n  \"start_line\": 278,\n  \"end_line\": 296,\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"d250f12902644004915d0c5133d5f7a9\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"867af3c83350466bcf2800868780b71c165597be3c612432e248a7f3a48bbcbb\",\n  \"basis\": \"agent_inference\",\n  \"description\": \"PersistentStorage implementation of the atomic all-or-rollback contract; early helper errors bypass batch consumption.\",\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"excerpt\": \"    fn write_atomically(&mut self, ops: Vec<StorageOp<T>>) -> StorageResult<()> {\\n        for op in ops {\\n            match op {\\n                StorageOp::AppendEntry(entry) => self.batch_append_entry(entry)?,\\n                StorageOp::AppendEntries(entries) => self.batch_append_entries(entries)?,\\n                StorageOp::AppendOnPrefix(from_idx, entries) => {\\n                    self.batch_append_on_prefix(from_idx, entries)?\\n                }\\n                StorageOp::SetPromise(bal) => self.batch_set_promise(bal)?,\\n                StorageOp::SetDecidedIndex(idx) => self.batch_set_decided_idx(idx)?,\\n                StorageOp::SetAcceptedRound(bal) => self.batch_set_accepted_round(bal)?,\\n                StorageOp::SetCompactedIdx(idx) => self.batch_set_compacted_idx(idx)?,\\n                StorageOp::Trim(idx) => self.batch_trim(idx)?,\\n                StorageOp::SetStopsign(ss) => self.batch_set_stopsign(ss)?,\\n                StorageOp::SetSnapshot(snap) => self.batch_set_snapshot(snap)?,\\n            }\\n        }\\n        Ok(self.db.write(std::mem::take(&mut self.write_batch))?)\\n    }\",\n  \"version\": 1\n}\nmonitor_results {\n  \"direct_check_id\": \"fe22cce109a743ca911c27ba656ac1d2\",\n  \"experiment_check_id\": \"eb1ca4d437f64ec8882a7005a78fb321\",\n  \"scope\": {\n    \"description\": \"PersistentStorage direct Storage API use on a live backend with a deterministic returned entry-serialization error after earlier operations were prepared.\",\n    \"assumptions\": [\n      \"Entry implements the required Entry, Serialize and Deserialize interfaces; serialization error is returned normally, not panic.\",\n      \"Successful database initialization and I/O outside the selected error; no concurrent writers or compaction.\"\n    ],\n    \"excluded\": [\n      \"No claim of a legal whole-cluster history continuing after a core storage panic.\",\n      \"No crash, power-loss durability, RocksDB write failure or application endpoint is tested.\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": {}\n  },\n  \"raw_log\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-05_09-27-12-omnipaxos-real-run/logs/eb1ca4d437f64ec8882a7005a78fb321/stdout.log\",\n  \"parsing_errors\": [],\n  \"prerequisites\": {\n    \"status\": \"matched\",\n    \"reason\": \"Declared prerequisites established\",\n    \"matched_indices\": [\n      0,\n      1\n    ],\n    \"alias_indices\": {\n      \"admitted\": 0,\n      \"failed\": 1\n    }\n  },\n  \"properties\": [\n    {\n      \"monitor_id\": \"monitor-rollback-live-length\",\n      \"checker_id\": \"rollback-live-length\",\n      \"outcome\": \"violated\",\n      \"witness_indices\": [\n        2\n      ],\n      \"valid_witness_indices\": [\n        2\n      ],\n      \"witness_complete\": true,\n      \"comparison_complete\": true,\n      \"missing_indices\": [],\n      \"evaluated_indices\": [\n        2\n      ],\n      \"outside_applicability_indices\": [],\n      \"correlations\": {\n        \"2\": {\n          \"status\": \"matched\",\n          \"reason\": \"Declared prerequisites established\",\n          \"matched_indices\": [\n            0,\n            1\n          ],\n          \"alias_indices\": {\n            \"admitted\": 0,\n            \"failed\": 1\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"diagnostics\": [],\n      \"limitations\": [],\n      \"reason\": \"Independent applicability, correlated prerequisites and fully observed result comparison\",\n      \"confirmed\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"monitor_id\": \"monitor-rollback-later-promise\",\n      \"checker_id\": \"rollback-later-promise\",\n      \"outcome\": \"violated\",\n      \"witness_indices\": [\n        4\n      ],\n      \"valid_witness_indices\": [\n        4\n      ],\n      \"witness_complete\": true,\n      \"comparison_complete\": true,\n      \"missing_indices\": [],\n      \"evaluated_indices\": [\n        4\n      ],\n      \"outside_applicability_indices\": [],\n      \"correlations\": {\n        \"4\": {\n          \"status\": \"matched\",\n          \"reason\": \"Declared prerequisites established\",\n          \"matched_indices\": [\n            0,\n            1\n          ],\n          \"alias_indices\": {\n            \"admitted\": 0,\n            \"failed\": 1\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"diagnostics\": [],\n      \"limitations\": [],\n      \"reason\": \"Independent applicability, correlated prerequisites and fully observed result comparison\",\n      \"confirmed\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"adaptations\": [\n    \"Use the public Entry serialization extension point to supply a returned error; all other entry values serialize normally.\",\n    \"Direct backend calls isolate the explicit Storage interface contract; no claim that the whole Paxos core continues after its storage panic.\",\n    \"Observe get_log_len from the live object and promise/entry data from backend public readers, then reopen as a diagnostic.\"\n  ],\n  \"conditions\": {\n    \"plan_uncertainties\": [\n      \"Compilation of the default omnipaxos target enables its existing persistent-storage dev dependency; preparation is not semantic evidence.\",\n      \"No cluster consequence, crash recovery failure, or RocksDB atomic-commit failure is inferred from a local backend contract violation.\",\n      \"Reopened state is retained as diagnostic corroboration of persistence after the later successful call, not a separate requirement.\"\n    ],\n    \"grounding_unresolved\": [],\n    \"review_limitations\": []\n  },\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"Direct oracle correspondence is unreviewed\"\n  ],\n  \"boundaries\": [\n    \"No claim of a legal whole-cluster history continuing after a core storage panic.\",\n    \"No crash, power-loss durability, RocksDB write failure or application endpoint is tested.\",\n    \"Compilation of the default omnipaxos target enables its existing persistent-storage dev dependency; preparation is not semantic evidence.\",\n    \"No cluster consequence, crash recovery failure, or RocksDB atomic-commit failure is inferred from a local backend contract violation.\",\n    \"Reopened state is retained as diagnostic corroboration of persistence after the later successful call, not a separate requirement.\"\n  ],\n  \"review_ids\": [],\n  \"open_issue_ids\": [],\n  \"correspondence\": null,\n  \"reviewed_complete\": false,\n  \"bounded_complete\": true,\n  \"confirmed\": false,\n  \"outcome\": \"violated\",\n  \"level\": \"implementation_test\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-storage-error-rollback\",\n  \"claim_version\": 1,\n  \"framework_revision\": \"audit-products-v50\",\n  \"finding_ids\": {\n    \"rollback-live-length\": \"3fe84c485dca414c85102f829c3c6bf3\",\n    \"rollback-later-promise\": \"673d9a81c62f47a79ec004daf8cd24d5\"\n  },\n  \"finding_id\": \"3fe84c485dca414c85102f829c3c6bf3\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The trusted run observed both rollback discrepancies. After the serialization error, the live length changed from `1` to `2`, while the stored promise remained `1`. A later transaction that only set the decided index committed promise `2` and entry `11` from the failed batch; both remained visible after reopen. This supports a backend rollback defect, not a whole-cluster safety claim.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\ns=dict(action='review',artifact_id='fe22cce109a743ca911c27ba656ac1d2',rationale='Review fixed version 1 against the actual returned-error and subsequent-transaction observations; preserve its direct Storage API scope.',review_items=[dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=['s-storage-contract','s-entry-contract','s-persistent-open','s-persistent-batch','s-persistent-atomic','s-persistent-read','s-storage-sync','s-follow','s-atomic-test-adapter'],rationale='Reviewed the fixed plan and harness under direct-checks/66acce1428c3477f8a6c0f0d1ea19ee1, version-1 claim/binding records, execution eb1ca4d437f64ec8882a7005a78fb321 and its raw CA_EVENT lines and monitor correlations. The Storage trait explicitly requires every operation or rollback and states that Err has restored pre-call state. The captured PersistentStorage implementation has ordinary Serialize bounds, propagates serialization errors with ?, and documents no mandatory discard/poisoning rule for a returned Err. A deterministic serializer that returns a normal error for one selected entry is an applicable use of that interface; it does not patch the backend, inject a fabricated successful return, or invoke undefined behavior. Nonselected values serialize as u64 and deserialize through the newtype; successful readback of initial entry 7 establishes this path. The database is unique within the authorized clean workspace, opened through PersistentStorageConfig::with_path and closed before cleanup, with no concurrent access or OS fault.\\\\n\\\\nThe admitted transaction starts from actual observed length 1, promise ballot number 1 and entry 7. Its input operations are SetPromise(ballot number 2), AppendEntry(11), then AppendEntry(999). The error event records the actual returned Err and actual invocation of the selected failing serializer, with text selected entry cannot be serialized. Both formal comparisons share this operation identity and causally preceding error event. The first reads live get_log_len after return and observes 2 \"'!= 1. Its promise remains 1 and first entry 7; those contrary observations are retained and show that initial persisted metadata was not changed merely because the cached cursor changed. The later call contains only SetDecidedIndex(0), returns Ok, and is unwrapped before the later result event. That event observes database promise number 2 != pre-call 1 and entries [7,11]. The independent-completed diagnostic is not a global prerequisite because it follows the immediate result, but the fixed driver and retained success event establish its execution and completion before the second result. No result-selected inputs or adaptive policy are used. The chosen identity is the single failed transaction, not its changed length or ballot. Promise comparison projects only ballot number, sufficient to witness inequality here because the failed transaction changes that component while the independent call cannot write any promise.'\"\\\\n\\\\nThe first discrepancy is live backend state: get_log_len uses next_log_key, not a count inferred by the test. The second is database state through get_promise, and the readback after closing and reopening additionally reports length 2, promise 2 and entries [7,11]. Reopen is diagnostic support for persisted leakage after the later successful transaction, not evidence that the first Err immediately persisted partial data. Source explains both outcomes: prior helpers queue batch operations and increment next_log_key; the later serializer error exits before mem::take, leaving both cursor and pending batch. The next write_atomically consumes that retained batch together with its own operation. This confirms the original local-state/retained-batch discriminator rather than a substituted database-atomicity hypothesis.\\\\n\\\\nExisting protections do not contradict the scoped comparison: one RocksDB commit can be atomic while the wrong earlier operations are retained for that commit; dropping/reopening immediately after Err might discard volatile pending state but is not the promised return-time rollback; core protocol paths panic on storage Err, so the test deliberately does not infer continued live core execution or a cluster endpoint. The mock atomic-storage adapter fails before its entire memory batch, so it does not exercise this mid-preparation serializer path. Parsing has no errors, both result comparisons are complete, and no issue was found in correspondence within the accepted scope.',limitations=['A direct PersistentStorage API contract violation under a controlled normal serialization error; no cluster decision divergence or post-panic core history is established.','No disk-write error, crash, power failure, concurrent writer, compaction or RocksDB durability setting is tested.','One transaction history with two observations of the same rollback responsibility; reopening occurs after an additional successful transaction.'],report_title='持久存储返回错误后仍保留失败事务的状态',report_answer='序列化返回 Err 后，公开读取的日志长度从 1 变成 2。随后仅设置 decided index 的独立事务，提交了失败事务中的 promise=2 和条目 11，重新打开数据库后仍可读到。该结果限定为 Storage 接口回滚违约，未证明集群级安全破坏。')],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['d2a273f49ba94c659cb424d58edeb657','b-persistent-transaction','b-persistent-view','fe22cce109a743ca911c27ba656ac1d2','eb1ca4d437f64ec8882a7005a78fb321','s-persistent-batch','s-persistent-atomic'],answered='The fixed Storage API history observed live length 2 after an Err from a transaction starting at length 1. A later successful transaction setting only decided index published the failed promise and entry; reopen retained them. Both comparisons violate the accepted rollback relation within this backend scope.',remaining=['Immediate discard/reopen and actual core panic recovery are independent histories outside this checked proposition.','Sparse node trim eligibility and configuration routing remain other sourced frontiers.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The observations distinguish cache mutation from later persistent leakage and retain the core panic boundary.',question_updates={'d2a273f49ba94c659cb424d58edeb657':dict(unknowns=[],resume_conditions=[])}))\np='persistent-review.json';json.dump(s,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));z=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+[p],capture_output=True,text=True);print(z.stdout);print(z.stderr)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\ns=dict(action='review',artifact_id='fe22cce109a743ca911c27ba656ac1d2',rationale='Review fixed version 1 against the actual returned-error and subsequent-transaction observations; preserve its direct Storage API scope.',review_items=[dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=['s-storage-contract','s-entry-contract','s-persistent-open','s-persistent-batch','s-persistent-atomic','s-persistent-read','s-storage-sync','s-follow','s-atomic-test-adapter'],rationale='Reviewed the fixed plan and harness under direct-checks/66acce1428c3477f8a6c0f0d1ea19ee1, version-1 claim/binding records, execution eb1ca4d437f64ec8882a7005a78fb321 and its raw CA_EVENT lines and monitor correlations. The Storage trait explicitly requires every operation or rollback and states that Err has restored pre-call state. The captured PersistentStorage implementation has ordinary Serialize bounds, propagates serialization errors with ?, and documents no mandatory discard/poisoning rule for a returned Err. A deterministic serializer that returns a normal error for one selected entry is an applicable use of that interface; it does not patch the backend, inject a fabricated successful return, or invoke undefined behavior. Nonselected values serialize as u64 and deserialize through the newtype; successful readback of initial entry 7 establishes this path. The database is unique within the authorized clean workspace, opened through PersistentStorageConfig::with_path and closed before cleanup, with no concurrent access or OS fault.\\\\n\\\\nThe admitted transaction starts from actual observed length 1, promise ballot number 1 and entry 7. Its input operations are SetPromise(ballot number 2), AppendEntry(11), then AppendEntry(999). The error event records the actual returned Err and actual invocation of the selected failing serializer, with text selected entry cannot be serialized. Both formal comparisons share this operation identity and causally preceding error event. The first reads live get_log_len after return and observes 2 \"'!= 1. Its promise remains 1 and first entry 7; those contrary observations are retained and show that initial persisted metadata was not changed merely because the cached cursor changed. The later call contains only SetDecidedIndex(0), returns Ok, and is unwrapped before the later result event. That event observes database promise number 2 != pre-call 1 and entries [7,11]. The independent-completed diagnostic is not a global prerequisite because it follows the immediate result, but the fixed driver and retained success event establish its execution and completion before the second result. No result-selected inputs or adaptive policy are used. The chosen identity is the single failed transaction, not its changed length or ballot. Promise comparison projects only ballot number, sufficient to witness inequality here because the failed transaction changes that component while the independent call cannot write any promise.'\"\\\\n\\\\nThe first discrepancy is live backend state: get_log_len uses next_log_key, not a count inferred by the test. The second is database state through get_promise, and the readback after closing and reopening additionally reports length 2, promise 2 and entries [7,11]. Reopen is diagnostic support for persisted leakage after the later successful transaction, not evidence that the first Err immediately persisted partial data. Source explains both outcomes: prior helpers queue batch operations and increment next_log_key; the later serializer error exits before mem::take, leaving both cursor and pending batch. The next write_atomically consumes that retained batch together with its own operation. This confirms the original local-state/retained-batch discriminator rather than a substituted database-atomicity hypothesis.\\\\n\\\\nExisting protections do not contradict the scoped comparison: one RocksDB commit can be atomic while the wrong earlier operations are retained for that commit; dropping/reopening immediately after Err might discard volatile pending state but is not the promised return-time rollback; core protocol paths panic on storage Err, so the test deliberately does not infer continued live core execution or a cluster endpoint. The mock atomic-storage adapter fails before its entire memory batch, so it does not exercise this mid-preparation serializer path. Parsing has no errors, both result comparisons are complete, and no issue was found in correspondence within the accepted scope.',limitations=['A direct PersistentStorage API contract violation under a controlled normal serialization error; no cluster decision divergence or post-panic core history is established.','No disk-write error, crash, power failure, concurrent writer, compaction or RocksDB durability setting is tested.','One transaction history with two observations of the same rollback responsibility; reopening occurs after an additional successful transaction.'],report_title='持久存储返回错误后仍保留失败事务的状态',report_answer='序列化返回 Err 后，公开读取的日志长度从 1 变成 2。随后仅设置 decided index 的独立事务，提交了失败事务中的 promise=2 和条目 11，重新打开数据库后仍可读到。该结果限定为 Storage 接口回滚违约，未证明集群级安全破坏。')],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['d2a273f49ba94c659cb424d58edeb657','b-persistent-transaction','b-persistent-view','fe22cce109a743ca911c27ba656ac1d2','eb1ca4d437f64ec8882a7005a78fb321','s-persistent-batch','s-persistent-atomic'],answered='The fixed Storage API history observed live length 2 after an Err from a transaction starting at length 1. A later successful transaction setting only decided index published the failed promise and entry; reopen retained them. Both comparisons violate the accepted rollback relation within this backend scope.',remaining=['Immediate discard/reopen and actual core panic recovery are independent histories outside this checked proposition.','Sparse node trim eligibility and configuration routing remain other sourced frontiers.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The observations distinguish cache mutation from later persistent leakage and retain the core panic boundary.',question_updates={'d2a273f49ba94c659cb424d58edeb657':dict(unknowns=[],resume_conditions=[])}))\np='persistent-review.json';json.dump(s,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));z=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+[p],capture_output=True,text=True);print(z.stdout);print(z.stderr)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"3e574b8052bb4708818b81b0db67ecc3\", \"audit_spec_version\": 3, \"elapsed_seconds\": 1699.9391072989997, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Validation against the state and bytes read; this is not acceptance, execution or evidence\"}\n\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
